; it-midi-macros — an embedded MIDI configuration, spelled and rebuilt.
;
; The fixture embeds a 4896-byte macro block that is not IT's default
; table: a macro in each family (the globals `start` and `note-on`, the
; parametric `sf0` and `sff` — the latter full to its 32nd byte with no
; terminator — and the fixed `z80` and `zff`). The block is the one
; opaque region a dump SPELLS, as `(it/midi (macro …) …)`, rather than
; references with a `(bin …)`, so the file tier a build reads back has
; no anchor to copy it from and has to carry the bytes itself.
;
; Rung 2 compares the block against its own anchor byte for byte. The
; `(build :kind it)` below goes the other way: the dumped tier read
; back through the bridge and written by the canonical writer, and its
; hash has to be the FIXTURE's — a build that zero-filled the block
; would hash differently here while still passing rung 1 over its own
; output. The `(dump)` is the skeleton the timeline tier derives; the
; `it/` tier itself is what the `(fixture …)` line already pins.
(read)
(roundtrip)
(dump)
(build :kind it)
